  "progress_note": "R2/S1 is accepted as research evidence. The operator ran the expanded nine-gate focused suite on 9aed4065: the original FPE gates, shared held-item state, third-person held-item presenter, performance gate and graphical scene-load all passed cleanly. In the graphical lab the selected item appears on the world avatar right hand and disappears when an empty hotbar slot is selected; Fix8 zero-stall behavior remains intact. S2 now replaces the single universal held-item box assumption with three research-only presentation services: ItemViewmodelCatalog resolves a visual descriptor from ItemDefinition id/tags/metadata with deterministic procedural fallback; HeldItemGripProfileCatalog resolves separate first-person and third-person transforms with metadata overrides; HeldItemVisualFactory builds the presentation proxy. CataloguedFirstPersonEmbodiment and CataloguedThirdPersonHeldItemPresenter consume the same descriptor/profile, while QuaterniusFirstPersonEmbodimentFix10 remains the fan-out from the shared transient HeldItemPresentationState. Heuristics currently distinguish beacon/signal, flashlight/torch, backpack, helmet and tool families; unknown definitions remain a generic box. Preferred world_scene_path is retained in the descriptor for later real-asset work but S2 deliberately uses bounded procedural primitives to avoid arbitrary asset-loading cost or scale assumptions. The catalogs and presenters explicitly own no Item Graph, network or gameplay transform truth. No accepted CH9.6 runtime file is modified. The previously unverified graphical equipment-drag result policy remains a non-blocking follow-up and is not claimed accepted.",
  "last_accepted_checkpoint": "FPE-R2 S1 RESEARCH ACCEPTED over CH9.6 accepted base e547ba52a440e72cc02c6bbe449edaf160bae7ab",
  "next_stage": "Operator updates the detached FPE worktree and runs RUN_FPE_RESEARCH_TESTS.ps1. New S2 gates: FPE R2 S2 item viewmodel catalog and FPE R2 S2 profiled presenters, followed by performance and graphical scene-load now bound to quaternius_first_person_embodiment_fix10.gd. Then run PLAY_FPE_RESEARCH.ps1. Graphical acceptance: occupied slots still switch instantly with no frame stall; first- and third-person show the same selected item family/profile; known differently classified definitions should have visibly different silhouette and/or grip orientation; C must not create a duplicate world proxy in first-person; empty slot clears both. Grip misalignment that still follows the correct hand is pose-tuning, not authority failure. After S2 acceptance proceed to R2/S3 real hand skeleton/pose library and then two-hand grip presentation. Canonical world grabbing remains a separate authority/network frontier.",
